{"text": "WHARFEDALE COACHLINES LTD\nMINUTES OF DISCIPLINARY HEARING - STRICTLY CONFIDENTIAL\n\nHeld at the depot, Unit 6, Snaygill Industrial Estate, Skipton BD23 2QR, on Thursday 6th November 2025 at 10.00am.\n\nPresent:  Shabnam Akhtar, Operations Manager (chair)\n          Gareth Moxon, PCV driver, payroll no. W0417\n          Derek Ainscough, Unite the Union branch rep (companion)\n          Lorna Peat, HR Administrator (notes)\n\n1. SA opened the hearing and confirmed GM had received the invite letter of 29/10/25 and the investigation pack. The hearing follows the ACAS Code of Practice.\n\n2. Allegations\n(a) That GM failed to tell the company about a conviction for drink-driving at Bradford Magistrates' Court in March 2019 when he applied in 2022, and answered \"No\" to the convictions question on the application form.\n(b) That on 14 October 2025 he drove vehicle YX19 KLO on the Ilkley school contract for 40 minutes beyond his permitted driving time (tachograph card DB04417712300010).\n\n3. GM's response\n(a) GM said the ban was 12 months, ended in 2020, and he believed it was \"spent\". DA referred to the Rehabilitation of Offenders Act 1974. SA said the form asks about any endorsement in the last five years and that the insurer must be told regardless. GM accepted he should have asked. His licence, no. MOXON710153G99LD, now shows no points.\n(b) GM said the relief driver did not turn up at Addingham and he could not leave 31 children on the roadside. He rang the depot on 01632 960122 twice and nobody picked up. SA confirmed the call log shows two missed calls from 07700 900164 at 15.52 and 15.58.\n\n4. Mitigation\nMr Ainscough said GM has three years' clean service. He asked the company to take into account that GM was diagnosed with sleep apnoea in the summer and now uses a CPAP machine; DVLA were notified and his D4 medical was passed on 2 September. GM added that his wife left in August and he has the two boys on his own, which is why he had been swapping shifts.\n\n5. Adjournment 10.48 to 11.20.\n\n6. Decision\n(a) Upheld. Final written warning, live for 12 months from today. GM to complete a new declaration; the insurer will be informed and any extra premium is the company's cost.\n(b) Not upheld as misconduct. Depot phone cover to be reviewed.\nGM's pay is unaffected (£15.90 per hour). The £250 Driver CPC training deduction agreed in July stands.\n\n7. Appeal: in writing to the Managing Director within five working days, i.e. by 13/11/2025. Outcome letter to GM's home address, 41 Gargrave Road, Skipton BD23 1PJ, and by email to gaz.moxon71@dalesmail.example.\n\nNotes taken by L. Peat. Gareth's date of birth for the insurer's form: 15.01.1971. NI no. NH 44 71 82 D.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "451 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Shabnam Akhtar", "Gareth Moxon", "Derek Ainscough", "Lorna Peat", "GM", "L. Peat", "Gareth", "gaz.moxon71"], "companies": ["WHARFEDALE COACHLINES LTD", "insurer", "driver CPC", "dalesmail"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Skipton", "Bradford", "Addingham"], "health": ["sleep apnoea", "CPAP machine", "D4 medical"], "sensitive": ["conviction", "drink-driving", "Rehabilitation of Offenders Act 1974", "wife", "two boys", "15.01.1971"], "names": ["Shabnam", "Gareth", "Lorna", "Derek"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.29999999701976776, "modelMs": 21955.69999999553, "topicMs": 29083.20000000298, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 25, "text": "WHARFEDALE COACHLINES LTD", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "WHARFEDALE COACHLINES LTD"}, {"start": 102, "end": 136, "text": "Unit 6, Snaygill Industrial Estate", "kind": "street", "sour